# OSPO Compliance & Legal Scrubbing Rules

**Trigger:** Apply these rules when the user asks to "prepare repo for open source", "check compliance", or "publish accelerator".
**⚠️ Recommended:** Use `/prepare-opensource` skill for interactive workflow.

**CRITICAL:** All required files MUST be placed at the top level of the repository root directory. This is a mandatory requirement from the Salesforce OSS template.

---

## 1. Internal Reference Scrubbing (Mandatory)

Before approving any code for publication, scan and flag/remove the following:

**Internal Domains:** References to `*.sfdc.sh`, `*.salesforce.com` (internal wiki links), or internal Git hosts (`git.soma.salesforce.com`).

**Internal Tools:** References to internal CI/CD systems (e.g., "GUS", "Grand Slam", internal Jenkins).

**Internal Comments:** Comments mentioning "TO DO (Internal)", employee names, or internal team codes.

**Non-Public Dependencies:** Ensure `sfdx-project.json` or `package.json` does not rely on private npm packages or internal Salesforce artifacts.

---

## 2. Mandatory Files Checklist (Top Level Only)

**REQUIREMENT:** All files listed below MUST exist at the top level of the repository root directory. Files in subdirectories will NOT satisfy this requirement.

Ensure the following files exist in the **root directory** (not in subdirectories). If missing, generate them:

### 2.1 LICENSE.txt (or LICENSE)

- **File Name:** `LICENSE.txt` (preferred) or `LICENSE` (acceptable)
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** Must contain the full text of the Apache License, version 2.0 (ALv2)
- **Template:** Use the standard Apache 2.0 license text from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/salesforce/oss-template/main/LICENSE.txt
- **Copyright Year:** Update to current year

### 2.2 CONTRIBUTING.md

- **File Name:** `CONTRIBUTING.md`
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** Standard file explaining how to contribute, report bugs, and rules of engagement
- **Template:** Based on https://raw.githubusercontent.com/salesforce/oss-template/main/CONTRIBUTING.md
- **Required Sections:**
  - Governance Model (Community Based, Salesforce Sponsored, or Published but not supported)
  - Getting started
  - Issues, requests & ideas
  - Contribution Checklist
  - Creating a Pull Request
  - Contributor License Agreement (CLA) reference
  - Code of Conduct reference
  - License reference

### 2.3 CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md

- **File Name:** `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** Salesforce Open Source Community Code of Conduct
- **Template:** Use exact content from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/salesforce/oss-template/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
- **Contact:** Must include `ossconduct@salesforce.com` for reporting

### 2.4 SECURITY.md

- **File Name:** `SECURITY.md`
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** Security policy and reporting instructions
- **Template:** Based on https://raw.githubusercontent.com/salesforce/oss-template/main/SECURITY.md
- **Required:** Security reporting email: `security@salesforce.com`

### 2.5 README.md

- **File Name:** `README.md`
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** Detailed, useful information about the project
- **Note:** Should contain detailed, useful information about the project (per OSS template requirements)

### 2.6 CODEOWNERS (Optional but Recommended)

- **File Name:** `CODEOWNERS`
- **Location:** Root directory only
- **Content:** File ownership and review assignments
- **Template:** Based on https://raw.githubusercontent.com/salesforce/oss-template/main/CODEOWNERS
- **Note:** Optional but recommended for larger projects

---

## 3. Copyright Headers

All source code files (Apex, LWC/JS, CSS, CMP, HTML) must include the standard Salesforce copyright header.

**Action:** If missing, add:

```apex
/*
 * Copyright (c) [YEAR], Salesforce, Inc.
 * All rights reserved.
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 * For full license text, see the LICENSE file in the repo root or https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0
 */
```

**For HTML/CMP files:**
```html
<!--
 Copyright (c) [YEAR], Salesforce, Inc.
 All rights reserved.
 SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 For full license text, see the LICENSE file in the repo root or https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0
-->
```

**File Types Requiring Headers:**
- `.cls` (Apex classes)
- `.trigger` (Apex triggers)
- `.js` (JavaScript/LWC)
- `.css` (Stylesheets)
- `.html` (HTML templates)
- `.cmp` (Aura components)
- `.js-meta.xml` (Metadata files - optional but recommended)

---

## 4. File Location Verification

**CRITICAL CHECK:** Before approving, verify that all required files are at the repository root:

```bash
# Verify files exist at root level
ls -la | grep -E "(LICENSE|CONTRIBUTING|CODE_OF_CONDUCT|SECURITY|README|CODEOWNERS)"
```

**Reject if:**
- Files are in subdirectories (e.g., `docs/LICENSE.md` or `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`)
- Files have incorrect names (e.g., `LICENCE` instead of `LICENSE`)
- Required files are missing

**Accept if:**
- All files are at root level
- File names match exactly (case-sensitive)
- Content matches templates

---

## 5. Content Verification

### 5.1 LICENSE.txt Verification
- [ ] Contains full Apache 2.0 license text
- [ ] Copyright year is current or appropriate
- [ ] No placeholder text remaining

### 5.2 CONTRIBUTING.md Verification
- [ ] Governance model selected and filled in
- [ ] All placeholder `{project_slug}` replaced
- [ ] CLA reference included
- [ ] Code of Conduct reference included
- [ ] License reference included

### 5.3 CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md Verification
- [ ] Exact Salesforce template content used
- [ ] Contact email `ossconduct@salesforce.com` present
- [ ] No modifications to standard text

### 5.4 SECURITY.md Verification
- [ ] Security reporting email `security@salesforce.com` present
- [ ] Appropriate security policy content

### 5.5 README.md Verification
- [ ] Contains detailed, useful project information
- [ ] Not just placeholder text
- [ ] Includes installation, usage, and contribution information

---

## 6. Final Verification Checklist

Before approving for publication, verify:

- [ ] All required files exist at **root level only**
- [ ] No internal references found (domains, tools, comments)
- [ ] All dependencies are public
- [ ] Copyright headers added to all source files
- [ ] LICENSE.txt/LICENSE contains full Apache 2.0 text
- [ ] CONTRIBUTING.md is complete and customized
- [ ] CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md matches Salesforce template
- [ ] SECURITY.md includes security@salesforce.com
- [ ] README.md contains detailed project information
- [ ] CODEOWNERS created (if applicable)

